TSM client.dll -- reTS's client DLL, built from source
======================================================

What this is
------------

ts\cl_dlls\client.dll is built from the reTS client source (cl_dll\), not from the stock TS
client plus a binary patch. The cloak fix that used to be a binary patch is now a source change
in cl_dll\view.cpp; its byte-level history is kept as an appendix, together with the stock
client it was applied to.

Deployed file : client.dll
Built by      : reTS\scripts\build-win32-dropin.ps1 with RETS_REBUILD=1
                (CMake, Win32, Release; target client)
Size          : 895488 bytes
SHA256        : EB8865E560331DD4D7D21B5F6C213B6C04E46244F750957C5F74E770249202E0
Source base   : goldsrc-net/the-specialists main through bd3f6c3c1aa3 (2026-10-29)

What the source build contains, beyond the stock client
-------------------------------------------------------

1. Local-player cloak alpha -- now in source

   The stock client has a per-frame block (around RVA 0x4d0af) that overwrites the local
   player's curstate rendermode/renderamt with a fixed third-person transparency taken from
   cl_thirdtransparency, so a server cloak (tsm_cloak_opacity) never reached the cloaker's own
   model. The binary patch added a pre-check that skipped that block when the server had already
   sent kRenderTransTexture with renderamt below 255. The same check is now in
   cl_dll\view.cpp, in the same block: bServerCloak skips the third-person fade, so the
   server's state survives to the studio draw. The hard reset (spectator/dead/first-person) is
   unchanged, and every non-cloak frame takes the original path.

   Verified in the built DLL: cmp [edi+0x2f8],2 / cmp [edi+0x2fc],0xff, then skip the fade.

2. Gunshot and ricochet pitch unclamped (upstream bd3f6c3c1aa3)

   cl_dll\ev_ts.cpp: the 255/1 clamp is gone from the gunshot, linked-fire and ricochet
   pitches. pitch = 100 + 300 * slow, 400 at normal speed; neither GoldSrc nor Xash caps pitch,
   so normal fire plays at 4x again instead of 2.55x.

3. Everything else reTS already had

   The reTS client is a recompilation of the whole TS client, so it also carries the third-person
   self-transparency fade, the predicted viewmodel body, the HUD and the rest of the reTS client
   work -- none of that is a patch on top of the stock DLL.

Building and deploying
----------------------

    cd reTS
    $env:RETS_REBUILD = '1'
    .\scripts\build-win32-dropin.ps1

writes binaries\ts\cl_dlls\client.dll (and the server's mp.dll). xash.bat's assemble step sets
RETS_REBUILD=1, so the H9XASH package takes this pair; export.bat's GoldSrc block copies the
same pair into export\ts\, and the Steam install's ts\cl_dlls\client.dll is this build too.

The older stock client with the binary cloak patch (865280 bytes, MD5
74fc8b3039032a31f7d81440bbde0e80) is kept in
backups\goldsrc_source_build_20261029\cl_dlls\client.dll and decompile_dll\client_patched_cloak.dll;
the appendix describes that build.

